  "summary": "Translation exercise: 16 English dialogue lines about holiday plans to say in Finnish, practising verb types 1–3 and the months (-kuussa), with vocabulary hints in brackets.",
  "transcript": "MILLOIN TE MENETTE LOMALLE?\n\nKuinka sanot seuraavat lauseet suomeksi:\n\n1.  Where are you (plural ”you”) travelling in the spring?\n\n2.  We are travelling to Thailand (Thaimaa).\n\n3.  Are you going in April or May?\n\n4.  In April. We will be there two weeks.\n\n5.  Where are you staying there? (to stay= asua)\n\n6.  In a nice, modern hotel in Phuket. We can swim in the sea in the morning. (kiva, moderni; hotelli; sea= meri > old Finnish word so last ”i” > E before endings)\n\n7.  How many rooms are there in the hotel? (”How many rooms in the hotel is?”)\n\n8.  Only 28. It is on a quiet road. And we can travel to the city centre by bus every hour. (only= vain; quiet= hiljainen, road= tie; city centre= keskusta)\n\n9.  Are you going on a holiday in autumn, too? (myös)\n\n10. Yes. We will drive to Norway in August and to France in September.\n\n11. Do you have a caravan? (asuntovaunu)\n\n12. No, but we are buying two large tents in July. My brother is selling them to us. (teltta)\n\n13. We are not holidaying until in November. (to holiday= lomailla; until= ennen kuin)\n\n14. Why? You always go on holiday in March.\n\n15. Yes but my wife has an operation in October. She will go to hospital and will be recovering three weeks. (operation= leikkaus; to recover= toipua)\n\n16. I have a bad flu and my wife had Covid in January. I hope that we will be OK and will not get ill again before we travel. (bad= paha, Covid= korona; to hope= toivoa; to be OK= olla kunnossa; to get ill= sairastua; before= ennen kuin)",
